WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:12.981
"What's your invention, Iggy?"

2
00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:14.102
asked Molly.

3
00:00:14.122 --> 00:00:19.206
"It's something to help people find their glasses," I explained.

4
00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:22.329
"Mrs. Romano will love it!"

5
00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.209
said Molly.

6
00:00:23.229 --> 00:00:26.472
"There's just one thing," I went on.

7
00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:33.685
"What?" asked Molly as we got in line for the bumpy slide on the playground.

8
00:00:36.506 --> 00:00:40.247
The slide was new, and everyone at our school was really excited about it.

9
00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:45.368
They were so excited, in fact, that the line was always very long.

10
00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:48.569
It was hard to wait for your turn sometimes.

11
00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:53.390
"I need to borrow your flower for my invention," I told Molly.

12
00:00:54.711 --> 00:00:56.451
She put her hand up to her headband.

13
00:00:56.471 --> 00:00:59.332
"My beautiful pink flower?"

14
00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:02.697
"I promise I'll give it back," I said.

15
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:06.159
"I just want to see if my idea works."

16
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.961
"I have to think about it," said Molly.

17
00:01:09.981 --> 00:01:12.883
"How long do you need to think?"

18
00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:13.943
I asked.

19
00:01:13.964 --> 00:01:18.266
"I have to think about that too," said Molly.

20
00:01:19.266 --> 00:01:20.207
I shook my head.

21
00:01:20.727 --> 00:01:22.788
She had to think about thinking about it?

22
00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:28.892
Just then a boy behind us bumped into Molly, and her flower fell off again.

23
00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:31.517
"No pushing in line!"

24
00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:32.698
called Mr.

25
00:01:32.738 --> 00:01:34.819
Dalmati, the recess helper.

26
00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.441
Molly picked up her flower.

27
00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:40.363
"I'm sorry," said the boy.

28
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:42.324
"I didn't mean to push.

29
00:01:42.684 --> 00:01:45.626
I'm just really excited about going down the bumpy slide."

30
00:01:48.288 --> 00:01:52.471
By the end of recess, Molly and I had gone down the slide only once.

31
00:01:54.973 --> 00:01:59.576
"I like the slide," I said, "but I miss running around the playground and playing games."

32
00:02:01.756 --> 00:02:06.598
"I wish we could stand in line and run around at the same time," said Molly.

33
00:02:06.618 --> 00:02:08.579
"Me too," I said.

34
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.440
After recess Mrs.

35
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.001
Romano told us she had a surprise.

36
00:02:14.021 --> 00:02:19.824
"Next week a special person is coming to visit our school," she announced.

37
00:02:19.844 --> 00:02:22.225
"His name is Mr.

38
00:02:22.325 --> 00:02:25.366
Bright, and he is an inventor."

39
00:02:25.386 --> 00:02:28.547
"I bet he gets lots of bright ideas!"

40
00:02:29.028 --> 00:02:29.748
Evan joked.

41
00:02:31.268 --> 00:02:32.468
All of the kids laughed.

42
00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:36.049
"Just like Iggy!"

43
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.150
added Molly.

44
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.250
"He's an inventor too."

45
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:43.132
"That's right," said Mrs.

46
00:02:43.212 --> 00:02:44.632
Romano, smiling at me.

47
00:02:44.652 --> 00:02:50.154
"But this time I want everyone to be thinking of ideas for inventions.

48
00:02:52.134 --> 00:02:58.276
Mr. Bright will choose the best one to include in his new book, The Kids' Invention Guide."

49
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.721
Jake moaned.

50
00:03:01.741 --> 00:03:05.223
"But how do we think up an invention, Mrs.

51
00:03:05.303 --> 00:03:07.105
Romano?" he asked.

52
00:03:08.306 --> 00:03:09.827
Mrs. Romano smiled.

53
00:03:09.847 --> 00:03:13.769
"Just look for a way to solve an everyday problem.

54
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.392
Problems are everywhere, right under your nose!"

55
00:03:19.153 --> 00:03:21.235
I leaned forward to whisper to Molly.

56
00:03:21.255 --> 00:03:24.377
"So can I borrow your flower?

57
00:03:24.717 --> 00:03:25.978
I'm going to need it."

58
00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:28.160
Molly turned around.

59
00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.101
"I'm still thinking about it, Iggy!"

60
00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:37.445
That afternoon Molly, Jenny, Josh, and I walked home from school together.

61
00:03:39.106 --> 00:03:42.649
The air was warm, and the trees were beginning to turn green.

62
00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.770
Jenny was sad.

63
00:03:46.551 --> 00:03:50.233
Sara, her best friend in third grade, was moving away.

64
00:03:50.253 --> 00:03:54.496
"I'm going to miss Sara," said Jenny.

65
00:03:55.488 --> 00:03:59.710
"We wear matching sweaters and matching shoes all the time.

66
00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.032
We even have matching glasses."

67
00:04:02.052 --> 00:04:06.034
"Is Sara moving far away?"

68
00:04:06.554 --> 00:04:07.275
asked Molly.

69
00:04:07.295 --> 00:04:11.677
"She's only moving ten blocks away," said Jenny.

70
00:04:11.697 --> 00:04:15.279
"But she'll be going to a different school now.

71
00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:18.341
We both cried when we said good-bye."

72
00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:21.523
"You'll be able to visit her," I said.

73
00:04:23.023 --> 00:04:23.724
Jenny nodded.

74
00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.337
Then I told Jenny and Josh about Mr.

75
00:04:26.397 --> 00:04:27.217
Bright's visit.

76
00:04:28.218 --> 00:04:32.299
The kids in Josh's class were writing down their ideas for inventions too.

77
00:04:32.319 --> 00:04:37.362
"I have a great idea for a new invention," I said, looking at Molly.

78
00:04:37.382 --> 00:04:41.703
"If someone will let me borrow her pink flower."

79
00:04:41.723 --> 00:04:48.807
"I've been thinking," said Molly as we approached a lady walking a little dog on a leash.

80
00:04:48.827 --> 00:04:54.872
"And I decided—" Molly never finished her sentence.

81
00:04:56.315 --> 00:04:58.579
Just then Jenny tripped over the dog's leash.

82
00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.665
Then Jenny went flying through the air!
